Hardware result
---------------

The branch was pushed at commit `7f80713` before the hardware submission.
The ANE passed the clean bring-up self-test.

Command:

  python3 tools/production-anec-probe.py /artifacts/chunk-13.anec --timeout 30

Observed probe metadata:

  content=0x59238000 task-stream=0xea2f8 td=0x274 td-count=1404 task-layout=original kernel=0x5914c800 workspace=0x68000 source=0x920000 output=0x90c000 source-nchw=(1, 2048, 1, 1, 64, 64) output-nchw=(1, 2048, 1, 1, 64, 64)

Observed result:

  TimeoutError: [Errno 110] Connection timed out
  tm execution failed w/ -110
  submit: execute returned -110

The exact task layout did not fix the full-graph timeout.

Next experiment
---------------

Fresh compiler artifacts have executed through explicit queue 1 in earlier
isolated tests. The failed full-graph probe used the KMD default queue. The
probe now accepts `--qid 1` so the next clean-boot submission can test that
single envelope difference.

